@media (max-width:640px){.fx-doc .page{padding:24px 16px 32px}.fx-doc header.brand{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start}.fx-doc header.brand .meta{text-align:left}.fx-doc h1.title{font-size:20pt}.fx-doc .cl.l2,.fx-doc .cl.sub{margin-left:14px}.fx-doc .cl.l3{margin-left:28px}.fx-doc .cl .n{min-width:34px}.fx-doc .sigwrap{grid-template-columns:1fr}.fx-doc .sigcell + .sigcell{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.fx-doc footer.foot{flex-direction:column}}
@media print{.fx-doc .page{max-width:100%;padding:0 12mm;margin:0;box-shadow:none}.fx-doc .execution{margin-top:20px}.fx-doc footer.foot{margin-top:14px;break-before:avoid;page-break-before:avoid}}</style><div class="fx-doc" data-doc="partner-agreement" data-version="2026-09-22"><div class="page"><header class="brand"><img class="logo-img" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Fixfy" width="102" height="36"><div class="meta">Getfixfy Ltd · Company No. 15406523<br>124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX</div></header><h1 class="title">PARTNER<span class="accent">AGREEMENT</span></h1><p class="version">Version 2026-09-22</p><p>THIS AGREEMENT (the <strong>“Agreement”</strong>) is made on the date it is accepted in the Fixfy platform, between:</p><p>(1) <strong>GETFIXFY LTD</strong>, a company registered in England and Wales under company number 15406523, whose registered office is at 124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX (<strong>“Fixfy”</strong>, <strong>“we”</strong>, <strong>“us”</strong> or <strong>“our”</strong>); and</p><p>(2) the independent business, whether a self-employed sole trader, a partnership or a company, whose details are recorded on the Fixfy account that accepts this Agreement (the <strong>“Partner”</strong>, <strong>“you”</strong> or <strong>“your”</strong>). Your legal or trading name, address, company number or UTR, VAT number (if you are registered) and bank details are the ones recorded on your Fixfy account.</p><div class="callout"><strong>How Fixfy works.</strong> Fixfy runs the operations behind service platforms, letting agents, landlords and businesses. We agree the work with our Clients and engage independent Partners to carry it out. You work with Fixfy as an independent business: you choose which Jobs to take, who carries them out and how you run your business.</div><p><strong>IT IS AGREED</strong> as follows:</p><h2 class="section" id="s1"><span class="n">1.</span>The Fixfy Platform and the Services</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c1.1"><span class="n">1.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy runs a platform made up of the Fixfy web platform on desktop, the Fixfy Trade mobile app and email (together, the <strong>“Platform”</strong>). Through it we receive and manage requests from our clients, including service platforms, letting agents, landlords, businesses and homeowners (the <strong>“Clients”</strong>), for services at properties they own, occupy or manage. These include end of tenancy, deep and after builders cleaning, painting and decorating, handyman repairs, carpentry, plumbing, electrical work, gardening and property safety certificates (the <strong>“Services”</strong>). Each visit or piece of work is a <strong>“Job”</strong>.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.2"><span class="n">1.2</span><div class="t">On the terms of this Agreement:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c1.2.1"><span class="n">1.2.1</span><div class="t">we may from time to time offer Jobs to you, in line with clause 3; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c1.2.2"><span class="n">1.2.2</span><div class="t">you agree, as an independent business, to carry out the Jobs you accept, yourself or through suitably skilled, experienced and authorised Partner Personnel.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.3"><span class="n">1.3</span><div class="t">By accepting this Agreement you confirm you have received the current Fixfy Partner Terms of Use (the <strong>“Terms of Use”</strong>), which set out our standards, rates, fees and procedures. The Terms of Use are not a contract on their own and we may change or withdraw them at any time. We will tell you about any change by email, in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform, and you agree to follow the Terms of Use as they stand at the time of each Job.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.4"><span class="n">1.4</span><div class="t">In this Agreement:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c1.4.1"><span class="n">1.4.1</span><div class="t">a <strong>“Booking”</strong> is a Job you have accepted, as explained in clause 3;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c1.4.2"><span class="n">1.4.2</span><div class="t"><strong>“Partner Personnel”</strong> means you, if you are an individual, and any individual you supply, engage, employ, contract with or otherwise make available to carry out a Booking on your behalf. References to you carrying out a Booking include Partner Personnel carrying it out; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c1.4.3"><span class="n">1.4.3</span><div class="t"><strong>“Job Details”</strong> means the information we give you on the Platform for each Job, including the Client's requirements, the scope of work, the address, access arrangements, the arrival window and the Partner Fee.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s2"><span class="n">2.</span>Your Relationship with Fixfy</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c2.1"><span class="n">2.1</span><div class="t">You are, and remain at all times, an independent business carrying on business on your own account. Nothing in this Agreement makes you or any Partner Personnel an employee, worker, agent or partner of Fixfy, and you must not present yourself or Partner Personnel as such. On site you attend on Fixfy's behalf as an independent Partner.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.2"><span class="n">2.2</span><div class="t">You are fully responsible for, and you will indemnify Fixfy against:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.2.1"><span class="n">2.2.1</span><div class="t">any income tax, corporation tax, National Insurance contributions, PAYE, apprenticeship levy, VAT and any other tax, deduction, contribution, assessment or claim arising from or in connection with the Services carried out by you or Partner Personnel, except where recovery is prohibited by law;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.2.2"><span class="n">2.2.2</span><div class="t">all reasonable costs, expenses and any penalty, fine or interest incurred or payable by Fixfy in connection with any liability under clause 2.2.1; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.2.3"><span class="n">2.2.3</span><div class="t">any liability arising from any employment-related claim, or any claim based on employee, worker, agency worker or similar status, brought against Fixfy by you or any Partner Personnel, and any employer-related liability for breach of immigration requirements relating to Partner Personnel.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.3"><span class="n">2.3</span><div class="t">Each party bears its own expenses in performing this Agreement. You supply your own tools, equipment, products and transport, unless the Job Details say otherwise.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.4"><span class="n">2.4</span><div class="t">Nothing in this Agreement creates an association, partnership, joint venture or agency between you and Fixfy. Unless we agree in writing, you have no authority to make any representation or commitment on Fixfy's behalf, including agreeing prices, extra work, refunds or compensation with a Client or resident.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.5"><span class="n">2.5</span><div class="t">This Agreement is not exclusive. You are free to provide services to anyone else and to have an interest in any other business, as long as doing so does not cause you to breach this Agreement or the Terms of Use, including clause 8.4.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.6"><span class="n">2.6</span><div class="t">It is a material condition of this Agreement that every member of Partner Personnel has, and can evidence, the right to work in the UK at all times, and that you have received and verified their right to work documents. In particular:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.6.1"><span class="n">2.6.1</span><div class="t">before anyone carries out a Booking, you must carry out a right to work check in line with the Home Office guidance in force at the time, and any follow-up checks that guidance requires;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.6.2"><span class="n">2.6.2</span><div class="t">you must follow any instruction we give you about immigration law compliance, including a request to audit your compliance, and that of Partner Personnel, with immigration law and right to work checks, and a request to verify the identity of any Partner Personnel;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.6.3"><span class="n">2.6.3</span><div class="t">you must follow any policy or procedure we introduce on immigration law compliance, including those our Clients require of us;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.6.4"><span class="n">2.6.4</span><div class="t">you must not subcontract a Booking to another business, except by supplying Partner Personnel in line with this Agreement, or with our express prior written permission. Where we give permission, you must make sure the subcontract contains obligations on the subcontractor equivalent to this clause 2.6, including right to work checks, audit rights and co-operation with the Home Office;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.6.5"><span class="n">2.6.5</span><div class="t">we may give information about you and Partner Personnel to the Home Office, and to any Client that must check its supply chain, including the structure of the contractual chain through which the Services are provided and the name, legal form, address and registration number of each business in it;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.6.6"><span class="n">2.6.6</span><div class="t">you must co-operate with any Home Office investigation into illegal working and give it any information it asks for;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.6.7"><span class="n">2.6.7</span><div class="t">you must tell us immediately if you know, or have reasonable cause to suspect, that any Partner Personnel is or may be working illegally; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c2.6.8"><span class="n">2.6.8</span><div class="t">we may take any step we consider necessary where illegal working is known or suspected, including suspending or ending this Agreement immediately, or requiring that the person does not carry out any Booking. Your own arrangements with Partner Personnel must allow you to take equivalent action.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.7"><span class="n">2.7</span><div class="t">Clause 2.6 is included only for immigration law and right to work compliance. Nothing in it creates or evidences an employment, worker or agency relationship between Fixfy and any Partner Personnel.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s3"><span class="n">3.</span>Job Offers and the Right to Decline</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c3.1"><span class="n">3.1</span><div class="t">When a Client asks us for a Service, we may offer the Job to you through the Platform: on the Fixfy web platform on desktop, in the Fixfy Trade app, by push notification or by email. You are free to accept or decline any Job. A Job you accept becomes a <strong>Booking</strong>.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.2"><span class="n">3.2</span><div class="t">If we assign a Job to you directly, you may decline it within 24 hours of being notified. If you do not, it becomes a Booking. A Job that starts less than 24 hours after we notify you only becomes a Booking once you accept it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.3"><span class="n">3.3</span><div class="t">Each Booking forms a separate contract between you and Fixfy on the terms of this Agreement, the Terms of Use and the Job Details. You do not have a contract with the Client, but you must follow the Client's requirements and site rules set out in the Job Details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.4"><span class="n">3.4</span><div class="t">We are under no obligation to offer you any Job, and you have no right to any Job, including Jobs for Clients or properties you have worked for before. You are under no obligation to accept any Job.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.5"><span class="n">3.5</span><div class="t">We may change, reallocate or cancel a Booking at any time if the Client asks us to or changes its plans, if we reasonably believe the Booking cannot be carried out safely or to standard, or if this Agreement ends. What we pay you in that case is set out in the Terms of Use.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s4"><span class="n">4.</span>Partner Personnel, Replacements and Cancellations</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c4.1"><span class="n">4.1</span><div class="t">You and Fixfy will tell each other about any absence, cancellation or inability to carry out a Booking in line with the Terms of Use. If you cancel a Booking with 24 hours' notice or less, or do not attend it, you will pay Fixfy the cancellation fee set out in the Terms of Use as liquidated damages. You agree that the fee is a reasonable and genuine pre-estimate of Fixfy's loss, which includes rearranging the Job at short notice, the charges our Client may apply to us and the harm to our relationship with the Client.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.2"><span class="n">4.2</span><div class="t">You are responsible for selecting, engaging, managing, supervising, paying and, where appropriate, replacing Partner Personnel. Subject to clause 4.3, you decide which Partner Personnel carry out each Booking, and you may replace them with other Partner Personnel without our approval.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.3"><span class="n">4.3</span><div class="t">Each time you supply someone to carry out a Booking, you warrant that:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c4.3.1"><span class="n">4.3.1</span><div class="t">they are at least 18 years old;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c4.3.2"><span class="n">4.3.2</span><div class="t">they hold a satisfactory Disclosure and Barring Service (<strong>“DBS”</strong>) check or an equivalent background check;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c4.3.3"><span class="n">4.3.3</span><div class="t">for cleaning, they have at least six months' cleaning experience, and for any other Service, they hold the accreditations and certifications set out in the Terms of Use for that Service;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c4.3.4"><span class="n">4.3.4</span><div class="t">they have the right to work in the UK, checked in line with clause 2.6; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c4.3.5"><span class="n">4.3.5</span><div class="t">as far as you are aware, having made reasonable enquiries, they have not previously been removed from Fixfy for serious misconduct or material breach, and have not behaved while carrying out services in a way that would have justified that.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.4"><span class="n">4.4</span><div class="t">You must make sure that all Partner Personnel are capable of carrying out the Booking and comply with this Agreement, the Terms of Use, the Job Details and the law. You remain fully liable for the acts and omissions of Partner Personnel as if they were your own, and you will indemnify Fixfy against any loss arising from them or from any claim brought by Partner Personnel, including legal fees incurred in defending such claims and any damages or compensation awarded.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.5"><span class="n">4.5</span><div class="t">You are wholly responsible for the pay, benefits, tax, National Insurance, insurance, training, equipment, conduct, health and safety and supervision of Partner Personnel, on whatever terms you agree with them. We pay you, not Partner Personnel, whoever carries out a Booking.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s5"><span class="n">5.</span>Client Keys and Access</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c5.1"><span class="n">5.1</span><div class="t">Clients may give you or Partner Personnel keys, fobs, key safe codes or other means of access to their properties (<strong>“Client Keys”</strong>). You are wholly responsible for keeping Client Keys safe and secure, and you are liable for any loss caused by Client Keys being lost, stolen, copied or damaged while you or Partner Personnel hold them, including the cost of replacing locks and keys. The rules for Client Keys are set out in the Terms of Use.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s6"><span class="n">6.</span>Fees and Payment</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c6.1"><span class="n">6.1</span><div class="t">For each Booking you are paid the fee shown in the Job Details when you accepted it (the <strong>“Partner Fee”</strong>). It is either a fixed price for the Job or an hourly, half day or day rate, paid for the time we approve. Approved materials are reimbursed on top, in line with the Terms of Use. The price the Client pays Fixfy is a matter between Fixfy and the Client.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.2"><span class="n">6.2</span><div class="t">A Booking becomes payable once you have completed it, submitted the completion report the Platform asks for, and we have approved it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.3"><span class="n">6.3</span><div class="t">We pay you by self-billing, under the separate Fixfy Self-Billing Agreement. Every two weeks we issue one self-bill listing the Bookings approved in that period and pay it to the bank account recorded on your Fixfy account, on the dates set out in the Terms of Use. You must not issue your own invoices for Bookings.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.4"><span class="n">6.4</span><div class="t">We may deduct from any payment due to you any amount you owe Fixfy under this Agreement or the Terms of Use, including cancellation fees, materials charged back and costs under clauses 8.3 and 10.2. Deductions are shown in a separate section of the self-bill, and each Booking is always shown at its full value.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.5"><span class="n">6.5</span><div class="t">We may change the Partner Fees we offer for future Jobs at any time. A change never affects a Booking you have already accepted.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.6"><span class="n">6.6</span><div class="t">All Partner Fees are inclusive of any VAT. If you are VAT registered, each self-bill shows the VAT included.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.7"><span class="n">6.7</span><div class="t">Any tip a Client or resident gives for a Booking belongs in full to the Partner Personnel who carried it out. If you pass a tip on through payroll, you bear any tax or National Insurance cost so that the person receives the full amount.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s7"><span class="n">7.</span>Termination and Suspension</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c7.1"><span class="n">7.1</span><div class="t">Either party may end this Agreement at any time and for any reason, with immediate effect, by telling the other in writing, by email, in the Fixfy Trade app or by telephone. Otherwise it continues indefinitely.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.2"><span class="n">7.2</span><div class="t">We may pause the Jobs we offer you, or remove you from Bookings, while any document we need is missing or out of date, while we look into a complaint or a quality or safety concern, or if you breach this Agreement or the Terms of Use.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.3"><span class="n">7.3</span><div class="t">When this Agreement ends: we may reallocate any Booking not yet carried out; you must immediately return any Client Keys and any property of Fixfy or a Client; and we will pay you for the Bookings you completed and we approved before the end, less any amount you owe us.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.4"><span class="n">7.4</span><div class="t">Clauses 2.2, 4.4, 5, 6.4, 8.4, 8.5, 10, 12 and 13, sections 12 and 13 of the Terms of Use, and any other provision intended to continue, survive the end of this Agreement.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s8"><span class="n">8.</span>Clients, Complaints and Remedial Work</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c8.1"><span class="n">8.1</span><div class="t">The relationship with the Client belongs to Fixfy. You must not agree prices, extra work, refunds or compensation with a Client or resident, or discuss your Partner Fee with them. Pass any such request to us through the Platform.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.2"><span class="n">8.2</span><div class="t">If a Client or resident complains about a Booking, we will look into it and decide how to resolve it with the Client. You must give us the information and help we reasonably ask for, within the time set out in the Terms of Use.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.3"><span class="n">8.3</span><div class="t">If work carried out under a Booking does not meet the Job Details or the standards in the Terms of Use, you will return to put it right at no extra charge, within the time set out in the Terms of Use. If you cannot or do not, we may arrange for someone else to do it and deduct the reasonable cost from your payments.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.4"><span class="n">8.4</span><div class="t">During this Agreement and for 12 months after it ends, you must not, and you must make sure Partner Personnel do not, directly or indirectly offer or provide services to any Client, or to any owner, landlord, tenant or resident of a property you attended through Fixfy, other than through Fixfy. This clause does not apply to anyone who was already your customer before you first met them through Fixfy.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.5"><span class="n">8.5</span><div class="t">If you breach clause 8.4, you will compensate Fixfy for the loss it suffers as a result, including the margin Fixfy would have earned on the work, and we may end this Agreement immediately.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s9"><span class="n">9.</span>Background Checks and Documents</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c9.1"><span class="n">9.1</span><div class="t">You warrant that you are an independent business carrying on business on your own account and that all Partner Personnel have the right to work and to carry out the Services in the UK.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.2"><span class="n">9.2</span><div class="t">You authorise Fixfy and its authorised agents to carry out the checks we reasonably consider necessary to verify your identity, business status and ability to carry out the Services, including the identity, right to work, DBS status, insurance and qualifications of Partner Personnel under clause 4.3. You agree to give us the relevant documents for you and all Partner Personnel, and updated documents whenever they change or expire and whenever we ask. These checks may include credit reference, Basic Disclosure and other background checks.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.3"><span class="n">9.3</span><div class="t">We keep your documents on file and may share them with a Client that needs to audit the supply chain for its Jobs.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s10"><span class="n">10.</span>Liability and Insurance</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c10.1"><span class="n">10.1</span><div class="t">You are solely responsible for any damage, loss or injury to any person or property that happens during or as a result of a Booking, whether caused negligently, recklessly or otherwise.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.2"><span class="n">10.2</span><div class="t">You will indemnify Fixfy against any loss, liability, cost (including reasonable legal costs), damages, charges or expenses Fixfy incurs as a result of a Booking carried out by you or Partner Personnel, including claims by Clients, residents or third parties, charges or penalties a Client applies to Fixfy, and the cost of remedial work.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.3"><span class="n">10.3</span><div class="t">You must hold the insurance set out in the Terms of Use throughout this Agreement and give us a copy of each certificate when you join and every time it renews. Fixfy's own insurance is for Fixfy's benefit only. It does not cover you or Partner Personnel and does not reduce your liability under this Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.4"><span class="n">10.4</span><div class="t">Fixfy's total liability to you under or in connection with this Agreement is limited to the Partner Fees due for Bookings you have completed and we have approved. We are not liable to you for any loss of profit, loss of business or indirect loss.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.5"><span class="n">10.5</span><div class="t">Nothing in this Agreement limits or excludes any party's liability for:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c10.5.1"><span class="n">10.5.1</span><div class="t">death or personal injury caused by its negligence;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c10.5.2"><span class="n">10.5.2</span><div class="t">fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation; or</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c10.5.3"><span class="n">10.5.3</span><div class="t">any other liability that cannot be limited or excluded by law.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s11"><span class="n">11.</span>Entire Agreement</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c11.1"><span class="n">11.1</span><div class="t">This Agreement, the Terms of Use, the Self-Billing Agreement and the Job Details of each Booking are the entire agreement between the parties and replace all earlier agreements and understandings between them, written or oral, on their subject matter. Each party agrees it has no remedy for any statement, representation, assurance or warranty, made innocently or negligently, that is not set out in them. Nothing in this clause limits or excludes liability for fraud, wilful misconduct or deliberate non-disclosure.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.2"><span class="n">11.2</span><div class="t">If there is a conflict, this Agreement takes priority over the Terms of Use, and the Job Details take priority over both on matters specific to that Booking, such as the scope of work, timing and Partner Fee.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s12"><span class="n">12.</span>Important Provisions</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c12.1"><span class="n">12.1</span><div class="t">A waiver of any right under this Agreement is only effective if it is in writing, and applies only in the circumstances for which it is given. No delay or failure by Fixfy in exercising any right or remedy operates as a waiver of it, and no single or partial exercise of a right or remedy prevents its further exercise. Rights and remedies under this Agreement are in addition to those provided by law.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.2"><span class="n">12.2</span><div class="t">If any provision, or part of a provision, of this Agreement is invalid, unenforceable or illegal, the rest of the Agreement is not affected. If it would be valid, enforceable and legal with part of it deleted, it applies with the minimum change needed to give effect to the commercial intention of the parties.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.3"><span class="n">12.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy may set off any sum due to you under this Agreement against any sum you owe Fixfy. Unless Fixfy agrees otherwise, you must pay any sum due to Fixfy in full, without any set-off or counterclaim.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.4"><span class="n">12.4</span><div class="t">You may not assign, transfer, charge, subcontract, declare a trust over or deal in any other way with any of your rights or obligations under this Agreement, except that you may supply Partner Personnel to carry out Bookings in line with clauses 2.6.4 and 4. Fixfy may assign, transfer, charge, subcontract or deal in any other way with any of its rights or obligations under this Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.5"><span class="n">12.5</span><div class="t">Fixfy may change this Agreement by giving you at least 14 days' notice by email, in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform. If you accept any Job after the change takes effect, you accept the changed Agreement from that date. If you do not want to accept the changes, your only remedy is to stop accepting Jobs from the date they take effect. We will keep the current version available on the Platform and keep a record of the date each version took effect.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.6"><span class="n">12.6</span><div class="t">No one other than a party to this Agreement, their successors and permitted assignees has any right to enforce any of its terms.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.7"><span class="n">12.7</span><div class="t">Notices under this Agreement may be given by email, to the address recorded on your Fixfy account or, for Fixfy, to support@getfixfy.com, or through the Platform.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.8"><span class="n">12.8</span><div class="t">Accepting this Agreement electronically on the Platform, including by signing on screen or tapping to accept, is as binding as signing it by hand. If you accept it for a business, you confirm you are authorised to do so.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s13"><span class="n">13.</span>Data Protection</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c13.1"><span class="n">13.1</span><div class="t">In this Agreement:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.1.1"><span class="n">13.1.1</span><div class="t"><strong>“Data Protection Legislation”</strong> has the meaning set out in section 3(9) of the Data Protection Act 2018;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.1.2"><span class="n">13.1.2</span><div class="t"><strong>“UK GDPR”</strong> has the meaning set out in section 3(10) of the Data Protection Act 2018;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.1.3"><span class="n">13.1.3</span><div class="t"><strong>“Losses”</strong> means losses, damages, liabilities, claims, costs and expenses, including fines, penalties, legal and other professional fees and expenses; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.1.4"><span class="n">13.1.4</span><div class="t">words and expressions defined in Article 4 of the UK GDPR have the same meaning in this Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.2"><span class="n">13.2</span><div class="t">Each party will comply with its obligations under Data Protection Legislation in connection with this Agreement. You will comply, and make sure Partner Personnel comply, with Data Protection Legislation and with any data protection, confidentiality and security obligations set out in the Terms of Use or the Job Details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.3"><span class="n">13.3</span><div class="t">If and to the extent the parties share personal data in connection with the Services, each party is a separate, and not a joint, controller. A party receiving shared personal data will:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.3.1"><span class="n">13.3.1</span><div class="t">process that personal data only for the purposes of and in connection with the Services, and not for any other purpose;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.3.2"><span class="n">13.3.2</span><div class="t">promptly tell the other party if it receives any complaint, notice or other communication about the processing of that personal data, or becomes aware of a personal data breach affecting it;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.3.3"><span class="n">13.3.3</span><div class="t">keep that personal data secure with appropriate technical and organisational measures, and delete it once it is no longer needed for the Booking, unless the law requires it to be kept; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.3.4"><span class="n">13.3.4</span><div class="t">make sure the information required under Articles 13 and 14 of the UK GDPR (a privacy notice) is available to any data subject of that personal data.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.4"><span class="n">13.4</span><div class="t">You will indemnify Fixfy on demand against all Losses incurred by Fixfy arising from or related to:</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.4.1"><span class="n">13.4.1</span><div class="t">your breach of your obligations under this clause 13;</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.4.2"><span class="n">13.4.2</span><div class="t">any breach of Data Protection Legislation by you or any Partner Personnel; and</div></div><div class="cl l2" id="c13.4.3"><span class="n">13.4.3</span><div class="t">any claim by a data subject arising from or related to such a breach.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s14"><span class="n">14.</span>Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c14.1"><span class="n">14.1</span><div class="t">This Agreement, and any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with it or its subject matter or formation (including non-contractual disputes or claims), is governed by the law of England and Wales.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.2"><span class="n">14.2</span><div class="t">The courts of England and Wales have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any such dispute or claim.</div></div><div class="execution"><h2>Signed</h2><p>This Agreement has been entered into on the date the Partner accepts it in the Fixfy platform.</p><div class="sigwrap"><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">Getfixfy Ltd</div><div class="script">Victor Braz de Souza</div><div class="sigcap">Signed by Victor Henrique Braz de Souza, Director</div><div class="sigcap">duly authorised, for and on behalf of Getfixfy Ltd</div></div><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">The Partner</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Signature</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Name, duly authorised, for and on behalf of the Partner</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Date</div></div></div><p class="signote">When you sign on screen or tap to accept in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform, your acceptance is recorded against this version of the Agreement and binds the Partner (clause 12.8).</p></div><footer class="foot"><span>Partner Agreement · Version 2026-09-22</span><span>Getfixfy Ltd · Company No. 15406523</span></footer></div></div>$fx$, false);

INSERT INTO public.contract_versions (contract_type, version, title, body_html, is_active)
VALUES ('terms_of_use', '2026-09-22', 'Partner Terms of Use', $fx$<style>.fx-doc{--navy:#020040;--coral:#ED4B00;--ink:#1c1c2b;--grey:#5d5d6e;--light:#f4f4f8;--line:#dcdce6;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);font-size:10.5pt;line-height:1.55;-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact;text-align:left}
