@media (max-width:640px){.fx-doc .page{padding:24px 16px 32px}.fx-doc header.brand{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start}.fx-doc header.brand .meta{text-align:left}.fx-doc h1.title{font-size:20pt}.fx-doc .cl.l2,.fx-doc .cl.sub{margin-left:14px}.fx-doc .cl.l3{margin-left:28px}.fx-doc .cl .n{min-width:34px}.fx-doc .sigwrap{grid-template-columns:1fr}.fx-doc .sigcell + .sigcell{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.fx-doc footer.foot{flex-direction:column}}
@media print{.fx-doc .page{max-width:100%;padding:0 12mm;margin:0;box-shadow:none}.fx-doc .execution{margin-top:20px}.fx-doc footer.foot{margin-top:14px;break-before:avoid;page-break-before:avoid}}</style><div class="fx-doc" data-doc="terms-of-use" data-version="2026-09-22"><div class="page"><header class="brand"><img class="logo-img" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Fixfy" width="102" height="36"><div class="meta">Getfixfy Ltd · Company No. 15406523<br>124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX</div></header><h1 class="title">PARTNER<span class="accent">TERMS OF USE</span></h1><p class="subtitle">Fixfy Operating Guide</p><p class="version">Version 2026-09-22</p><p>The terms, standards, rates and fees in these Partner Terms of Use (the <strong>“Terms of Use”</strong>) apply to every Partner Agreement between <strong>GETFIXFY LTD</strong> (company number 15406523, registered office 124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX) (<strong>“Fixfy”</strong>, <strong>“we”</strong> or <strong>“us”</strong>) and the independent Partners who carry out Jobs for Fixfy. Each of those agreements is the <strong>“Partner Agreement”</strong>.</p><p>As a Partner, you agree to follow, and to make sure all Partner Personnel follow, the rules, procedures and standards in these Terms of Use as they stand from time to time. Words defined in the Partner Agreement have the same meaning here. References to you doing something include Partner Personnel doing it. These Terms of Use are not a contract on their own, and Fixfy may change or withdraw them at any time, as explained in clause 1.3 of the Partner Agreement.</p><div class="callout"><strong>In short.</strong> You choose the Jobs you take. We send them through the Fixfy web platform on desktop, the Fixfy Trade app and email. You are paid the Partner Fee shown on each Job, every two weeks, by self-billing. We don't charge you to join or to receive Jobs. The only fee we charge is <strong>£50 for a Booking you cancel with 24 hours' notice or less, or don't attend.</strong></div><h2 class="section" id="s1"><span class="n">1.</span>Fees and Payment</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c1.1"><span class="n">1.1</span><div class="t"><strong>Partner Fee.</strong> For each Booking you are paid the Partner Fee shown in the Job Details when you accept it. It is always labelled in front of the amount: <strong>Fixed</strong> (a set price for the Job), <strong>Hourly</strong> (a rate per hour, paid for the hours we approve), <strong>Half day</strong> or <strong>Day rate</strong>. For example: “Fixed · £120.00” or “Hourly · £40.00/hr”.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.2"><span class="n">1.2</span><div class="t"><strong>No joining fee.</strong> Fixfy does not charge you to join the Platform, to stay on it or to receive Jobs. The only fee we charge you is the late cancellation fee in section 3.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.3"><span class="n">1.3</span><div class="t"><strong>Payment periods.</strong> We pay in fortnightly periods, each running from a Monday to the second Sunday after it. For each period we issue one self-bill listing every Booking you completed and we approved by the end of that Sunday, and we pay it on the Friday after the period closes. For example, a period that closes on Sunday the 13th is paid on Friday the 18th.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.4"><span class="n">1.4</span><div class="t">Bookings still waiting for approval when a period closes move to the self-bill of the period in which we approve them.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.5"><span class="n">1.5</span><div class="t"><strong>Bank account.</strong> We pay into a UK bank account in the Partner's name, as recorded on your Fixfy account. If the Partner is a company, it must be the company's business account. We cannot pay until we have valid bank details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.6"><span class="n">1.6</span><div class="t"><strong>What the self-bill shows.</strong> Each self-bill shows your Bookings at their full value, any materials reimbursed and, in a separate section, any deductions, such as late cancellation fees or materials charged back. If anything on a self-bill looks wrong, tell us within 14 days, as set out in the Self-Billing Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.7"><span class="n">1.7</span><div class="t"><strong>Materials.</strong> Fixed-price Jobs include the consumables you normally need for that kind of work. If a Job needs materials that are not included, check with us through the Platform before you buy them. We reimburse approved materials at cost when you record them in the completion report with a photo of the receipt.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.8"><span class="n">1.8</span><div class="t">All amounts in these Terms of Use are inclusive of any VAT.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s2"><span class="n">2.</span>Availability and Job Offers</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c2.1"><span class="n">2.1</span><div class="t">Keep your Fixfy account up to date in the Fixfy Trade app, including: the postcodes and areas you cover; the days and times you can work; the Services you offer and the Partner Personnel who carry them out; your documents (insurance, accreditations, right to work and DBS); and your business, tax and bank details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.2"><span class="n">2.2</span><div class="t">We send Job offers and Booking updates through the Platform: the Fixfy web platform on desktop, the Fixfy Trade app (including push notifications) and email. Keep notifications switched on and your email address up to date.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.3"><span class="n">2.3</span><div class="t">You may accept or decline any Job offer. If we assign a Job to you directly, you may decline it within 24 hours of being notified; after that it becomes a Booking. A Job that starts less than 24 hours after we notify you only becomes a Booking once you accept it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.4"><span class="n">2.4</span><div class="t">Some Jobs ask for your price first. Your quote is an offer to carry out the work for that amount, and it becomes a Booking only if we confirm it.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c2.5"><span class="n">2.5</span><div class="t">Every day at around 17:00 UK time we email you your Bookings for the next day, in the order you should attend them. Check it, and tell us straight away if anything is wrong.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s3"><span class="n">3.</span>Cancellations and Absences by You</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c3.1"><span class="n">3.1</span><div class="t">Once you have accepted a Booking, you may cancel it, or tell us you cannot supply Partner Personnel for it, free of charge if you give us more than 24 hours' notice before the arrival window starts. Cancel in the Fixfy Trade app or by contacting the Fixfy office.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.2"><span class="n">3.2</span><div class="t">If you cancel with 24 hours' notice or less, or you do not attend, you pay Fixfy a cancellation fee of <strong>£50</strong> for each Booking, as liquidated damages under clause 4.1 of the Partner Agreement. We deduct it from your next self-bill.</div></div><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th>When you tell us</th><th>Cancellation fee</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>More than 24 hours before the arrival window starts</td><td>£0</td></tr><tr><td>24 hours or less before the arrival window starts</td><td>£50</td></tr><tr><td>You do not attend, or you do not tell us at all</td><td>£50</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="cl l1" id="c3.3"><span class="n">3.3</span><div class="t">The cancellation fee covers Fixfy's loss from the cancellation itself. It does not cover Client property or materials lost, damaged or wasted as a result, which you still owe.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.4"><span class="n">3.4</span><div class="t">You are not paid for any part of a Booking you do not carry out.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.5"><span class="n">3.5</span><div class="t">If you are going to arrive after the start of the arrival window, tell us through the app as soon as you know, and in any case before the window starts. If you arrive after the window ends without having told us, we may treat the Booking as one you did not attend.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.6"><span class="n">3.6</span><div class="t">Give us at least one week's notice if you will not be able to carry out Bookings you have accepted because of a holiday, business closure, staffing or any other planned reason.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c3.7"><span class="n">3.7</span><div class="t">Repeated late cancellations or missed Bookings may lead us to offer you fewer Jobs, pause your account or end the Partner Agreement.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s4"><span class="n">4.</span>Cancellations and Changes by Fixfy or Clients</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c4.1"><span class="n">4.1</span><div class="t">We may change, reallocate or cancel a Booking if the Client asks us to, or in the other cases in clause 3.5 of the Partner Agreement. We will give you as much notice as we can. Apart from section 4.2, we are not liable to you for lost fees, Partner Personnel costs or travel costs.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.2"><span class="n">4.2</span><div class="t">We pay you a call-out of <strong>£25</strong>, unless the Job Details say a different amount, if:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">the Client cancels the Booking with 24 hours' notice or less; or</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">you cannot carry out the Booking because of the Client, for example because nobody lets you in or the property is not ready, and you tell us through the app while you are at the property, with a photo.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.3"><span class="n">4.3</span><div class="t">You agree the call-out is a genuine pre-estimate of your loss, and you will not claim anything further from Fixfy or the Client for that cancellation.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s5"><span class="n">5.</span>Partner Personnel and Accreditations</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c5.1"><span class="n">5.1</span><div class="t">You are responsible for selecting, engaging, managing, supervising, paying and, where appropriate, replacing the Partner Personnel who carry out Bookings. You decide who carries out each Booking and may replace them without our approval, as long as the replacement meets section 5.2.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.2"><span class="n">5.2</span><div class="t">Before anyone carries out a Booking, you must make sure that:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">they are at least 18 years old;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">they hold a satisfactory DBS check (at least a basic DBS) or an equivalent background check;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">for cleaning, they have at least six months' cleaning experience;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">for any other Service, they hold the accreditations in section 5.5; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">their right to work has been checked in line with section 15.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.3"><span class="n">5.3</span><div class="t">Before someone attends a Booking for the first time, tell us their name through the app or by email, so we can tell the Client who is coming, and keep their right to work and DBS evidence ready to give us.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.4"><span class="n">5.4</span><div class="t">You are wholly responsible for paying, training, equipping, insuring, supervising and managing Partner Personnel. Fixfy invoices and pays you under the normal arrangements, and never pays Partner Personnel directly.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.5"><span class="n">5.5</span><div class="t"><strong>Minimum accreditations.</strong> These are the minimum for each Service. You also warrant that you hold any other certification, accreditation, insurance and training required by law or by good industry practice.</div></div><table class="grid"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Minimum accreditation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cleaning (end of tenancy, deep, after builders)</td><td>At least six months' cleaning experience</td></tr><tr><td>Handyman repairs, carpentry, painting and decorating</td><td>Asbestos awareness training (Control of Asbestos Regulations 2012, regulation 10)</td></tr><tr><td>Plumbing</td><td>NVQ Level 2 or 3 in Plumbing; G3 unvented hot water certification where the Job involves unvented systems</td></tr><tr><td>Electrical work and Electrical Installation Condition Reports (EICR)</td><td>Membership of a Competent Person Scheme (NICEIC, NAPIT, ELECSA or Stroma)</td></tr><tr><td>Gas work, boiler services and gas safety certificates</td><td>Gas Safe registration for the work carried out (CCN1 and CENWAT as a minimum); G3 where relevant</td></tr><tr><td>Appliance repair</td><td>City &amp; Guilds NVQ Level 3 in domestic appliance servicing; Gas Safe and F-Gas certification where the Job involves them</td></tr><tr><td>Energy Performance Certificates (EPC)</td><td>Accredited Domestic Energy Assessor with a government-approved accreditation scheme</td></tr><tr><td>PAT testing</td><td>Qualified and competent to test portable appliances (for example City &amp; Guilds 2377)</td></tr><tr><td>Fire risk assessments</td><td>Competent assessor with a recognised fire risk assessment qualification or registration</td></tr><tr><td>Fire alarms, emergency lighting and extinguishers</td><td>Competent engineer working to BS 5839, BS 5266 or BS 5306 as relevant</td></tr><tr><td>Gardening and waste removal</td><td>Waste carrier registration if you take any waste away</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 class="section" id="s6"><span class="n">6.</span>Carrying Out the Job</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c6.1"><span class="n">6.1</span><div class="t"><strong>Arrival.</strong> Arrive within the arrival window shown in the Job Details, or at the set time where the Job has one.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.2"><span class="n">6.2</span><div class="t"><strong>Scope.</strong> Carry out the work in the Job Details, following our checklists (such as the end of tenancy checklist) and the Client's requirements. Do extra work only if we approve it through the Platform before you start. We do not pay for work we have not approved.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.3"><span class="n">6.3</span><div class="t"><strong>Reports and photos.</strong> Submit the start and completion reports in the Fixfy Trade app, with the photos the app asks for, before you leave the property. The completion report is what makes a Booking payable. Photos must show the property and the work only: never people, documents, post or anything else that identifies the resident.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.4"><span class="n">6.4</span><div class="t"><strong>Problems on site.</strong> If you find damage, a safety issue, an access problem or work that is not in the scope, stop and tell us through the app straight away, with photos.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.5"><span class="n">6.5</span><div class="t"><strong>Remedial visits.</strong> If the Client reports within 7 days of the Booking that something in the Job Details or checklist was not done, or not done to standard, you will return to put it right at no extra charge, at a time we agree with the Client, normally within 48 hours of us telling you. If you cannot, clause 8.3 of the Partner Agreement applies.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.6"><span class="n">6.6</span><div class="t"><strong>Conduct.</strong> On site you represent Fixfy. Be courteous, punctual and tidy; do not smoke, vape or drink alcohol at the property; do not bring anyone who is not carrying out the Booking; and do not hand out your own business cards, prices or contact details.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.7"><span class="n">6.7</span><div class="t"><strong>Waste.</strong> Only take waste away from a property if the Job includes it and you hold a waste carrier registration, and always dispose of it lawfully.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s7"><span class="n">7.</span>Client Keys and Access</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c7.1"><span class="n">7.1</span><div class="t">When you receive Client Keys, you must:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">tell us straight away that you are holding them;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">tag them with the unique code we give you; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">make sure the Client's name, address and other identifying details are never written on or near them.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.2"><span class="n">7.2</span><div class="t">Unless we authorise it in writing, you must not give or lend Client Keys to anyone other than the Partner Personnel carrying out the Booking, and you must not copy them. Never share or write down key safe or access codes.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.3"><span class="n">7.3</span><div class="t">Tell us immediately if any Client Keys held by you or Partner Personnel are lost, stolen or damaged.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.4"><span class="n">7.4</span><div class="t">Whenever we or the Client ask, hand over all Client Keys immediately to Fixfy, the Client or whoever we tell you, at your own cost.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c7.5"><span class="n">7.5</span><div class="t">If you do not follow this section, we may withhold any payment due to you until you do.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s8"><span class="n">8.</span>Equipment and Supplies</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c8.1"><span class="n">8.1</span><div class="t">You provide your own tools, equipment and products, unless the Job Details say otherwise. Do not use the Client's own supplies unless the Job Details say you may.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.2"><span class="n">8.2</span><div class="t">Everything you use must be fit for purpose and safe, and used in line with the manufacturer's instructions, normal industry practice and the rules on hazardous substances (COSHH).</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s9"><span class="n">9.</span>Quality and Ratings</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c9.1"><span class="n">9.1</span><div class="t">We track quality on every Booking, including Client feedback and ratings, report completeness, punctuality, cancellations and complaints. You agree to carry out the Services professionally and in a way that seeks the best possible feedback.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.2"><span class="n">9.2</span><div class="t">Client ratings and feedback are outside our control, and we are not liable for any loss you suffer because of them.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c9.3"><span class="n">9.3</span><div class="t">If your quality, reliability or complaint record falls below our standards, we may offer you fewer Jobs, pause your account or end the Partner Agreement.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s10"><span class="n">10.</span>Insurance</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c10.1"><span class="n">10.1</span><div class="t">Throughout the Partner Agreement you must hold:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">public liability insurance of at least £1,000,000 for each claim, covering all the Services you carry out and all Partner Personnel;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">employers' liability insurance of at least £5,000,000 if you employ anyone, as the law requires; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">any other insurance the law requires for your Services, and professional indemnity insurance where you issue certificates or reports (for example EICR, gas safety, EPC or fire risk assessments).</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.2"><span class="n">10.2</span><div class="t">Upload your insurance certificates to your Fixfy account when you join and every time they renew. We may pause Jobs while a certificate is missing or out of date.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.3"><span class="n">10.3</span><div class="t">Fixfy's own insurance is maintained for Fixfy's benefit only. You are not a named insured under it and it does not cover you or Partner Personnel for the Services.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c10.4"><span class="n">10.4</span><div class="t">If you become aware of anything that could lead to a claim, tell us without delay, and give us and our insurers the information, help and signed documents we reasonably ask for.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s11"><span class="n">11.</span>Damage, Complaints and Disputes</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c11.1"><span class="n">11.1</span><div class="t">If anything is broken or damaged during a Booking, you must: tell us through the app as soon as possible, with photos and details; not agree anything with the Client or resident yourself; and answer our questions within 48 hours.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.2"><span class="n">11.2</span><div class="t">We decide how to resolve any complaint or dispute with the Client, which may include a remedial visit, a repair, a replacement or a refund. Where the cause is your work or the conduct of Partner Personnel, you are responsible for the reasonable cost, and we may deduct it from your payments after telling you the amount and the reason.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c11.3"><span class="n">11.3</span><div class="t">If you disagree with a deduction, tell us within 14 days and we will review it with you in good faith.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s12"><span class="n">12.</span>Intellectual Property and Photos</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c12.1"><span class="n">12.1</span><div class="t"><strong>“Intellectual Property Rights”</strong> means patents, copyright and related rights, trade marks, business and domain names, goodwill and the right to sue for passing off, rights in designs, software and databases, rights in confidential information and know-how, and all similar rights anywhere in the world, whether registered or not.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.2"><span class="n">12.2</span><div class="t">All Intellectual Property Rights in Fixfy's business, including the Fixfy name and logo and the Platform, belong to Fixfy. You may not use them for any purpose without our written permission, during or after the Partner Agreement.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.3"><span class="n">12.3</span><div class="t">You may not use the name, logo or brand of any Client, including the platforms we work with, for any purpose.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c12.4"><span class="n">12.4</span><div class="t">Photos, reports and other material that you or Partner Personnel create for a Booking belong to Fixfy. You assign, and will make sure Partner Personnel assign, all rights in them to Fixfy, and waive any moral rights in them. We may use them to evidence the work to Clients and, with personal details removed, in our own materials. You may not use them for any other purpose.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s13"><span class="n">13.</span>Confidential Information</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c13.1"><span class="n">13.1</span><div class="t"><strong>“Confidential Information”</strong> means any information, in any form, about the business, Clients, residents, properties, prices, systems, affairs or finances of Fixfy or of any Client, including information you create, receive or obtain in connection with the Partner Agreement, whether or not it is marked confidential.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.2"><span class="n">13.2</span><div class="t">You will not, and will make sure Partner Personnel do not, use or disclose Confidential Information to anyone, except to carry out Bookings, either during the Partner Agreement or at any time after it ends. You will use your best endeavours to prevent its publication or disclosure.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.3"><span class="n">13.3</span><div class="t">These restrictions do not apply to any use or disclosure authorised by Fixfy or required by law, or to information that is or becomes public other than through your breach.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.4"><span class="n">13.4</span><div class="t">If a Client asks, you will, and will make sure Partner Personnel will, sign a separate confidentiality agreement for that Client's Jobs.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c13.5"><span class="n">13.5</span><div class="t">Nothing in the Partner Agreement or these Terms of Use prevents you or Partner Personnel from making a protected disclosure, co-operating with or giving information to any regulatory, supervisory, investigatory or prosecuting body, reporting an offence to the police, reporting anything the law requires you to report, or discussing these matters with professional advisers or medical professionals who owe a duty of confidentiality.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s14"><span class="n">14.</span>Data Protection</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c14.1"><span class="n">14.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy holds and processes data about you and Partner Personnel for legal, contractual and legitimate business purposes, including: identity, contact, business, tax and bank details; right to work, DBS, insurance and accreditation documents; and activity on the Platform, such as Job acceptances, check-in times, reports and photos. Where needed, this includes special category and criminal records data, for example DBS results needed to meet legal and Client requirements, and right to work documents that may reveal nationality.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.2"><span class="n">14.2</span><div class="t">You will, and will make sure Partner Personnel will, comply with Data Protection Legislation and with our data protection policy when handling personal data of Clients, residents or anyone else in connection with a Booking. Use resident details only to carry out the Booking, and delete them once it is complete.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.3"><span class="n">14.3</span><div class="t">We may share with Clients and residents the name and, where the Client asks, the photo of the Partner Personnel attending, and your business details where a Client needs to check its supply chain.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c14.4"><span class="n">14.4</span><div class="t">Our privacy notice for Partners explains how we use personal data. You can ask for it at any time at support@getfixfy.com.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s15"><span class="n">15.</span>Right to Work Checks</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c15.1"><span class="n">15.1</span><div class="t">Before anyone carries out a Booking, you must check their right to work in line with the Home Office guidance in force at the time, including any follow-up check, and make sure nobody starts a Booking before that check has been completed.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c15.2"><span class="n">15.2</span><div class="t">You must tell us immediately about any change in the immigration status or personal circumstances of any Partner Personnel that may affect their right to work in the UK.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c15.3"><span class="n">15.3</span><div class="t">We may take any step we consider necessary for right to work compliance, including cancelling or stopping a Booking immediately where we reasonably believe the person attending does not have the right to work in the UK.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c15.4"><span class="n">15.4</span><div class="t">You must comply with any request from us to audit your compliance, and that of Partner Personnel, with immigration law and right to work checks, including any request to verify the identity of Partner Personnel, and you must co-operate with any Home Office investigation into illegal working.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c15.5"><span class="n">15.5</span><div class="t">When we ask, you must give us written confirmation that the prescribed right to work checks have been carried out on all Partner Personnel who carry out, or are due to carry out, Bookings, with the date of each check and, where relevant, when the follow-up check is due. Keep copies of all right to work documents and give them to us promptly when we ask, for any audit or Home Office investigation.</div></div><div class="execution"><h2>Signed</h2><p>By signing or accepting in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform, the Partner confirms it has read these Terms of Use and agrees to follow them, and to make sure all Partner Personnel follow them.</p><div class="sigwrap"><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">Issued by Getfixfy Ltd</div><div class="script">Victor Braz de Souza</div><div class="sigcap">Signed by Victor Henrique Braz de Souza, Director</div><div class="sigcap">duly authorised, for and on behalf of Getfixfy Ltd</div></div><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">Accepted by the Partner</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Signature</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Name, duly authorised, for and on behalf of the Partner</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Date</div></div></div><p class="signote">Your acceptance is recorded on the Platform against this version of the Terms of Use.</p></div><footer class="foot"><span>Partner Terms of Use · Version 2026-09-22</span><span>Getfixfy Ltd · Company No. 15406523</span></footer></div></div>$fx$, false);

INSERT INTO public.contract_versions (contract_type, version, title, body_html, is_active)
VALUES ('self_bill_agreement', '2026-09-22', 'Self-Billing Agreement', $fx$<style>.fx-doc{--navy:#020040;--coral:#ED4B00;--ink:#1c1c2b;--grey:#5d5d6e;--light:#f4f4f8;--line:#dcdce6;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);font-size:10.5pt;line-height:1.55;-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact;text-align:left}
.fx-doc *{box-sizing:border-box}
.fx-doc .page{background:#fff;max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:44px 52px 56px}
.fx-doc header.brand{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;border-bottom:3px solid var(--coral);padding-bottom:12px}
.fx-doc .logo-img{display:block;height:36px;width:auto;max-width:100%}
.fx-doc header.brand .meta{font-size:8.5pt;color:var(--grey);text-align:right;line-height:1.45}
.fx-doc h1.title{font-size:24pt;color:var(--navy);font-weight:800;margin:26px 0 6px;line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.fx-doc h1.title .accent{color:var(--coral);display:block}
.fx-doc .subtitle{font-size:11pt;color:var(--navy);font-weight:700;margin:2px 0 0}
.fx-doc .version{font-size:8.5pt;color:var(--grey);margin:6px 0 16px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em}
.fx-doc p{margin:8px 0}
.fx-doc strong{color:var(--navy)}
.fx-doc .callout{background:var(--light);border-left:4px solid var(--coral);padding:12px 16px;margin:16px 0;font-size:10pt}
.fx-doc h2.section{font-size:12.5pt;color:var(--navy);font-weight:700;margin:26px 0 8px;break-after:avoid;page-break-after:avoid}
.fx-doc h2.section .n{color:var(--coral);display:inline-block;min-width:30px}
.fx-doc .cl{display:flex;gap:10px;margin:6px 0}
.fx-doc .cl .n{flex:0 0 auto;min-width:40px;color:var(--navy);font-weight:700;font-size:9.5pt;padding-top:1px}
.fx-doc .cl .t{flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0}
.fx-doc .cl.l2{margin-left:40px}
.fx-doc .cl.l3{margin-left:80px}
.fx-doc .cl.sub{margin-left:40px}
.fx-doc .cl.sub .n,.fx-doc .cl.l2 .n,.fx-doc .cl.l3 .n{min-width:48px;font-weight:600;color:var(--grey)}
.fx-doc table.grid{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:10px 0 12px;font-size:9.5pt}
.fx-doc table.grid th,.fx-doc table.grid td{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:8px 10px;vertical-align:top;text-align:left}
.fx-doc table.grid th{background:var(--light);color:var(--navy);font-weight:700}
.fx-doc table.grid td:last-child{width:46%}
.fx-doc .execution{margin-top:34px;break-inside:avoid;page-break-inside:avoid}
.fx-doc .execution h2{font-size:15pt;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 10px}
.fx-doc .sigwrap{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:12px}
.fx-doc .sigcell{padding:16px}
.fx-doc .sigcell + .sigcell{border-left:1px solid var(--line)}
.fx-doc .sigcell .h{font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:6px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em}
.fx-doc .script{font-family:"Brush Script MT","Snell Roundhand","Segoe Script",cursive;font-size:24pt;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.1;min-height:38px;margin:6px 0 2px}
.fx-doc .sigline{border-bottom:1.5px solid var(--navy);height:38px;margin-top:8px}
.fx-doc .sigcap{font-size:8.5pt;color:var(--grey);margin-top:3px}
.fx-doc .signote{font-size:9pt;color:var(--grey);margin-top:10px}
.fx-doc footer.foot{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:36px;padding-top:8px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;font-size:8.5pt;color:var(--grey)}
.ob-contract .fx-doc .page{max-width:none;margin:0;padding:6px 4px 16px;box-shadow:none}
@media (max-width:640px){.fx-doc .page{padding:24px 16px 32px}.fx-doc header.brand{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start}.fx-doc header.brand .meta{text-align:left}.fx-doc h1.title{font-size:20pt}.fx-doc .cl.l2,.fx-doc .cl.sub{margin-left:14px}.fx-doc .cl.l3{margin-left:28px}.fx-doc .cl .n{min-width:34px}.fx-doc .sigwrap{grid-template-columns:1fr}.fx-doc .sigcell + .sigcell{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.fx-doc footer.foot{flex-direction:column}}
@media print{.fx-doc .page{max-width:100%;padding:0 12mm;margin:0;box-shadow:none}.fx-doc .execution{margin-top:20px}.fx-doc footer.foot{margin-top:14px;break-before:avoid;page-break-before:avoid}}</style><div class="fx-doc" data-doc="self-billing" data-version="2026-09-22"><div class="page"><header class="brand"><img class="logo-img" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Fixfy" width="102" height="36"><div class="meta">Getfixfy Ltd · Company No. 15406523<br>124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX</div></header><h1 class="title">SELF-BILLING<span class="accent">AGREEMENT</span></h1><p class="version">Version 2026-09-22</p><p>This Self-Billing Agreement (the <strong>“Self-Billing Agreement”</strong>) is made on the date it is accepted in the Fixfy platform, between:</p><p>(1) <strong>GETFIXFY LTD</strong>, a company registered in England and Wales under company number 15406523, whose registered office is at 124 City Road, London EC1V 2NX (<strong>“Fixfy”</strong>, the self-biller); and</p><p>(2) the independent business whose details are recorded on the Fixfy account that accepts this Self-Billing Agreement (the <strong>“Partner”</strong>, the supplier). The Partner's name, address, company number or UTR and VAT registration number (if registered) are the ones recorded on that account.</p><p>It applies to the Jobs the Partner carries out for Fixfy under the Partner Agreement. Words defined in the Partner Agreement and the Partner Terms of Use have the same meaning here.</p><div class="callout"><strong>What self-billing means.</strong> Fixfy prepares your invoice for you. Every two weeks we issue one self-bill listing the Bookings you completed, and we pay it. You don't need to send us invoices, and you must not send your own invoice for the same work.</div><h2 class="section" id="s1"><span class="n">1.</span>The Agreement to Self-Bill</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c1.1"><span class="n">1.1</span><div class="t">The Partner agrees that Fixfy will issue self-billed invoices (<strong>“self-bills”</strong>) for all supplies the Partner makes to Fixfy under the Partner Agreement, for as long as this Self-Billing Agreement lasts.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c1.2"><span class="n">1.2</span><div class="t">This Self-Billing Agreement starts on the date the Partner accepts it and lasts for 12 months. It then renews for further periods of 12 months unless it ends earlier under clause 8.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s2"><span class="n">2.</span>Fixfy's Commitments</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c2.1"><span class="n">2.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy agrees to:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">issue a self-bill for each fortnightly payment period set out in the Terms of Use, covering every Booking the Partner completed and Fixfy approved in that period;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">show on each self-bill: a unique sequential number; the date of issue; Fixfy's name and address, and VAT registration number if Fixfy is registered; the Partner's name and address, and VAT registration number if the Partner is registered; each Booking with its reference, date, property and amount; any materials reimbursed; any deductions, shown separately; and the total payable;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">where the Partner is VAT registered, show the rate and amount of VAT included, and the statement “The VAT shown is your output tax due to HMRC”;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">send each self-bill to the Partner by email or through the Platform, and keep a copy;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">keep a record of the Partner's name, address and, if registered, VAT registration number; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(f)</span><div class="t">make a new self-billing agreement with the Partner if the Partner's VAT registration number changes.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s3"><span class="n">3.</span>The Partner's Commitments</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c3.1"><span class="n">3.1</span><div class="t">The Partner agrees to:</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(a)</span><div class="t">accept the self-bills Fixfy issues for the Partner's supplies until this Self-Billing Agreement ends;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(b)</span><div class="t">not issue its own sales invoices or VAT invoices for the supplies covered by this Self-Billing Agreement;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(c)</span><div class="t">tell Fixfy immediately, in writing, if it registers for VAT, stops being registered for VAT, changes its VAT registration number, changes its legal form (for example from sole trader to limited company), or sells or transfers its business or any part of it;</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(d)</span><div class="t">keep its business name, address, tax details and bank details on its Fixfy account accurate and up to date; and</div></div><div class="cl sub"><span class="n">(e)</span><div class="t">keep a copy of every self-bill it receives.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s4"><span class="n">4.</span>Queries and Corrections</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c4.1"><span class="n">4.1</span><div class="t">If the Partner believes a self-bill is wrong, it must tell Fixfy within 14 days of receiving it, through the Platform or by email to support@getfixfy.com, explaining what is wrong.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.2"><span class="n">4.2</span><div class="t">Fixfy will review the query in good faith. Any agreed correction is made on the next self-bill as a separate, clearly described line, or by issuing a credit note or a supplementary self-bill.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c4.3"><span class="n">4.3</span><div class="t">A self-bill the Partner does not query within 14 days is treated as accepted. This does not prevent either party from correcting an obvious error later.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s5"><span class="n">5.</span>Deductions</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c5.1"><span class="n">5.1</span><div class="t">Fixfy may deduct from a self-bill any amount the Partner owes Fixfy under the Partner Agreement or the Terms of Use, including late cancellation fees, materials charged back, and the cost of remedial work or damage determined under the Terms of Use.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c5.2"><span class="n">5.2</span><div class="t">Deductions are shown in a separate Deductions section of the self-bill, with a description of each one. Each Booking is always shown at its full value.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s6"><span class="n">6.</span>VAT and Tax</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c6.1"><span class="n">6.1</span><div class="t">All Partner Fees and other amounts on a self-bill are inclusive of any VAT due on them.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.2"><span class="n">6.2</span><div class="t">The Partner is responsible for its own income tax, National Insurance, corporation tax and VAT, and for declaring the amounts on its self-bills to HMRC. Fixfy does not deduct tax from payments, except under clause 6.3.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c6.3"><span class="n">6.3</span><div class="t">Where a Booking is construction work within the Construction Industry Scheme (<strong>“CIS”</strong>), such as painting and decorating, repairs or building work, Fixfy will verify the Partner with HMRC before paying and make any deduction HMRC requires, at the rate HMRC confirms. The deduction is shown on the self-bill, and Fixfy will give the Partner a CIS payment and deduction statement for each tax month in which a deduction is made.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s7"><span class="n">7.</span>Records</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c7.1"><span class="n">7.1</span><div class="t">Each party will keep its copies of self-bills and related records for at least six years.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s8"><span class="n">8.</span>Ending this Self-Billing Agreement</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c8.1"><span class="n">8.1</span><div class="t">Either party may end this Self-Billing Agreement at any time by telling the other in writing, including by email or through the Platform.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.2"><span class="n">8.2</span><div class="t">This Self-Billing Agreement ends automatically when the Partner Agreement ends, or if the Partner's VAT registration changes in a way that requires a new self-billing agreement. Fixfy will still issue the final self-bill for Bookings completed before it ends.</div></div><div class="cl l1" id="c8.3"><span class="n">8.3</span><div class="t">If the Partner continues to supply Fixfy after this Self-Billing Agreement ends, it must issue its own invoices until a new self-billing agreement is in place.</div></div><h2 class="section" id="s9"><span class="n">9.</span>Governing Law</h2><div class="cl l1" id="c9.1"><span class="n">9.1</span><div class="t">This Self-Billing Agreement is governed by the law of England and Wales and operates in line with HMRC's self-billing rules (VAT Notice 700/62, as updated from time to time). The courts of England and Wales have exclusive jurisdiction.</div></div><div class="execution"><h2>Signed</h2><p>By signing or accepting in the Fixfy Trade app or on the Platform, the Partner agrees to this Self-Billing Agreement and confirms that the details on its Fixfy account are correct.</p><div class="sigwrap"><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">Getfixfy Ltd (self-biller)</div><div class="script">Victor Braz de Souza</div><div class="sigcap">Signed by Victor Henrique Braz de Souza, Director</div><div class="sigcap">duly authorised, for and on behalf of Getfixfy Ltd</div></div><div class="sigcell"><div class="h">The Partner (supplier)</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Signature</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Name, duly authorised, for and on behalf of the Partner</div><div class="sigline"></div><div class="sigcap">Date</div></div></div><p class="signote">Your acceptance is recorded on the Platform against this version of the Self-Billing Agreement.</p></div><footer class="foot"><span>Self-Billing Agreement · Version 2026-09-22</span><span>Getfixfy Ltd · Company No. 15406523</span></footer></div></div>$fx$, false);


-- Uma versão ativa por tipo: desliga a antiga e liga a nova.
UPDATE public.contract_versions SET is_active = false
 WHERE contract_type IN ('contractor_service_agreement','terms_of_use','self_bill_agreement')
   AND is_active = true AND version <> '2026-09-22';
UPDATE public.contract_versions SET is_active = true
 WHERE version = '2026-09-22'
   AND contract_type IN ('contractor_service_agreement','terms_of_use','self_bill_agreement');
